      "title": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in Behavioral and Organizational Science (22960)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in Behavioral and Organizational Science (22960) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in Behavioral and Organizational Science (22960) Requisition ID 22960 - Posted 09/02/2026 - Type of position (2) - Area of Activity (5) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Postdoctoral researcher will be a member of the Department of Organizational Behavior of HEC Lausanne. The OB Department provides a stimulating, interdisciplinary research environment. The members of the department have backgrounds in various fields including social and industrial-organizational psychology, the cognitive and decision sciences, human evolutionary ecology, management, and economics. We publish in top-tier journals in different areas. The research profiles of department members can be found here . Job information Expected starting date:    January 1st, 2027, or a mutually acceptable alternative Contract duration:           The initial contract is one year and is renewable for a further two-year term. Total of 3 years. Place of work:                 University of Lausanne, Faculty of Economics and Business, Lausanne/Dorigny Type of position:              75% Salary:                            According to legal stipulations here Your responsibilities 70% the workload will be devoted to personal research. 30% of the workload will be dedicated to teaching (one 3-ECTS course in the first year and two 3-ECTS courses in the second year). Depending on your preference teaching in English or in French is possible. Your qualifications We are looking for someone with the following profile: PhD in Management, Economics, Psychology, Sociology, Biology, Physics, or another discipline that offers ways into the study of human behavior in organizations. You must have the proven ability to publish in leading international journals and to have requisite teaching experience at the university level. Strong focus on behavioral research in any area of the behavioral sciences, including but not limited to organizational behavior, decision making, human resource management, cognitive science, industrial psychology, economics, leadership, negotiation, human evolution, or related fields. You must be able to teach courses related to organizational behavior, broadly defined, in the Bachelor’s and Master's program. The specific course topics will be defined later during the process and be based on the successful candidate's expertise. The following list represents candidate topics for teaching, though the list is not meant to exclude other courses that may better fit the candidate’s background: “Human Resource Management”, “Organizational Behavior”, “Contemporary Topics in HR Management”, “The Future of Work”, “Organizational Culture and Behavior Change”, the “Psychology of Judgment and Decision-making”, “and “Introduction to Human Behavior, Affect, and Cognition”. Your application Deadline: September 30th, 2026 Please submit the following documents through the UNIL applications platform. •    Letter of motivation •    Curriculum Vitae with references •    Samples of scholarly work •    Contact of three references Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be considered. We thank you for your understanding. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information The Department Director will serve as the point of contact and act as managing director for the position in what concerns administrative matters. Any question may be addressed to Prof. Julian Marewski ( Julian.marewski@unil.ch ), Head of the OB Department, or to Vanessa Zirek ( vanessa.zirek@unil.ch ), Executive Assistant of the OB Department Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
