    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22927&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=MqVOJaeoN3APO%2flh%2fVEWrlAmhKgIZ69zWj4GfpPWhX0%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Origin of Life (22927)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Origin of Life (22927) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: PhD position in Origin of Life (22927) Requisition ID 22927 - Posted 08/31/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work NCCR GENESIS - Fully funded PhD position The National Centre of Competence in Research NCCR Genesis is a research infrastructure project funded by SNSF focussing on exploring the emergence of life in the Universe. This interdisciplinary research infrastructure brings together physicists, earth and planetary scientists, chemists and biologists to understand the conditions and the mechanisms that enable life to emerge. Developing reliable methods to detect reliable traces of life (biosignatures)– whether through remote sensing or direct onsite measurements– requires significant innovation. These challenges demand close collaboration across physics, biology, chemistry and the earth sciences. NCCR Genesis does not aim to provide answers in all fields, but to drive innovative research and achieve decisive progress. Details on NCCR Genesis are available on its website https://nccr-genesis.ch . NCCR Genesis is deeply committed to equality, diversity and inclusion. Our aim is to cultivate a respectful and fair work culture with equal access to professional development and support for all. We strongly encourage applications from under-represented groups. Presentation We are seeking a full-time PhD student to join the Environmental Fluid Mechanics laboratory at UNIL (led by Professor Pietro de Anna, at the Institute of Earth Science) and the Laboratory of Statistical Biophysics at EPFL (led by Professor Paolo De Los Rios, at the Institute of Physics). This post is fully founded by the Swiss National Science foundation (NCCR Genesis). Job information Expected start date in position : Fall 2026 or upon mutual agreement Contract length : 1 year + 2 + 1,  maximum 4 years Activity rate : 100 % Workplace : Lausanne Dorigny - Géopolis Your responsibilities The successful candidate will work on a PhD thesis on chemical reaction networks in controlled and structured environments. This will be achieved by developing novel microfluidics devices to understand how non-equilibrium and non-homogeneous environments influence the network kinetics and the consequent abundance of reaction products. The physical and chemical properties will be tuned independently. Using pumps, pressure controllers and time-lapse video-microscopy, flow experiments through microfluidics structures will be performed to quantify the local reaction kinetics. Experimental results will be compared with theoretical models based on reaction-diffusion equations. The candidate will be trained in cutting-edge microfluidics and numerical models. The research work will involve collaborations with a suite of international colleagues across Europe and the US. Most of the PhD student’s time will be dedicated to research, but contributing to some teaching activities can be discussed, including the additional possibility of supervising master students. Your qualifications Master degree (or be near completion) in Physics or Mechanical Engineering or Civil & Environmental Engineering or Chemical Physics/Physical Chemistry or related discipline with a good understanding of at least one of the following topics: i) chemical physics, ii) statistical mechanics, iii) transport phenomena (dispersion, mixing and reactive transport), iv) microfluidics and video-microscopy. Written and spoken English are required, but working knowledge of French (the local language in Lausanne) is not necessary. Commitment to research based on experimental, numerical and modeling approaches. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work The Environmental Fluid Mechanics Laboratory is an established facility, located at the Institute of Earth Sciences (ISTE) at the University of Lausanne, equipped with state-of-the-art technology including fully automated microscopes, dedicated clean room for micro-fabrication and a microbiology laboratory. The University of Lausanne is sharing the campus with EPFL, making the local environment very dynamical and stimulating. More information about the Environmental Fluid Mechanics Laboratory can be found at www.pietrodeanna.org . The Laboratoriy of Statistical Biophysics (LBS), at the Institute of Physics and Institute of Bioengineering of EPFL, studies how biological and prebiotic molecular systems organize, maintain and remodel matter away from thermodynamic equilibrium. We combine statistical physics, polymer theory, kinetic modeling, reaction-network theory, bioinformatics, machine learning and experiments to connect molecular mechanisms with emergent organization across scales. A major focus is protein homeostasis, in particular how molecular chaperones such as Hsp70 use ATP to generate forces, reshape protein conformational ensembles, reverse aggregation and stabilize the proteome under stress. In parallel, we study nonequilibrium chemical reaction networks, asking how fluxes, gradients, interfaces and spatial heterogeneity can bias chemical pathways and promote the emergence of complex molecular products. More information about the Laboratory of Statistical Biophysics can be found at http://lbs.epfl.ch . Contact for further information Any questions can be directed to Prof. Pietro de Anna (pietro.deanna@unil.ch) or Paolo De Los Rios (paolo.delosrios@epfl.ch). Your application Deadline : 06.09.2026 Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22955&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=MqVOJaeoN3APO%2flh%2fVEWrlAmhKgIZ69zWj4GfpPWhX0%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher SNSF in Information Systems (22955)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher SNSF in Information Systems (22955) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher SNSF in Information Systems (22955) Requisition ID 22955 - Posted 08/27/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Visual Collaboration Lab is opening a full-time postdoctoral position in sustainability research (related to Management of Information Systems – MIS and/or Management) to do research at the intersection of multidisciplinary collaboration, sustainability and wicked problem. This senior (postdoc) position is available within the framework of the interdisciplinary project “ A Digital Inquiry Platform for wicked problems: the case of sustainability assessment of business models ”, funded by the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF). Job information Expected start date in position : Autumn 2026 / to be agreed Contract length : 1 year, renewable 1 year, maximum 2 years Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Lausanne, Campus of Dorigny Your responsibilities In your activities, you will have to conduct innovative research into how to address the wicked problem of sustainability (related to environmental, societal and/or economic aspects) based on multidisciplinary collaboration. The main purpose is to reflect on how to help multidisciplinary teams to address wicked problems. In this endeavor, you will collaborate with UI/UX designers, developers, and multidisciplinary researchers. You should therefore be interested in the human aspect of sustainability and multidisciplinary approaches. 100% of your time will be dedicated to the research. The successful candidate will be supervised by Prof. Stephanie Missonier. Your qualifications In order to complete our team, we are looking for someone with the following skills : PhD in IS / Management or related field anchored around sustainability or human aspect of sustainability. Willingness to do research in the fields of sustainability, multidisciplinary collaboration and wicked problems Strong skills in qualitative research and Design Science Research Strong relational and communication skills Interest in multidisciplinary projects Fluency in English or French, with a good knowledge of the other language What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Prof. Stephanie Missonier Stephanie.missonier@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 15.09.2026 Please include: A curriculum vitae including (3 pages max.), A cover letter, List of publications, The name of up to three references willing to write recommendation letters, A synthesis of your PhD thesis and an electronic version of a recent research project write-up (e.g., PhD thesis, scientific publications). Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. UNIL is committed to promoting gender equality and strongly encourages applications from female candidates. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22957&selected_lang=fr_FR&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=MqVOJaeoN3APO%2flh%2fVEWrlAmhKgIZ69zWj4GfpPWhX0%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Un·e coordinateur·trice de programme (22957)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Un·e coordinateur·trice de programme (22957) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Un·e coordinateur·trice de programme (22957) Requisition ID 22957 - Posted 08/25/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction La Formation Continue UNIL-EPFL (FCUE) est une fondation qui regroupe les activités de formation continue de l’Université de Lausanne (UNIL) et de l’École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL). Elle propose, aux professionnel·le·s et entreprises, plus de 300 formations dans des domaines aussi variés que : Science & Technique, Santé-Social, Sciences humaines, Gestion, Économie & Droit et Administration publique. Présentation Afin de compléter son équipe, la FCUE est à la recherche d’un·e coordinateur·trice de programme pour les formations continues interuniversitaires en Management, Ressources Humaines et Carrières (MRHC) à 60%. Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : 1er janvier 2027 ou à convenir Durée du contrat : une année, renouvelable (et pouvant évoluer en CDI) Taux d'activité : 60% Lieu de travail : Campus de Dorigny et possibilité de télétravail Vos activités Sous l’autorité fonctionnelle du président du Comité directeur des formations, avec délégation à la directrice exécutive, vous assurez la coordination et la gestion des programmes de formation, ainsi que l’encadrement des participant·e·s et des intervenant·e·s. Vos principales tâches sont les suivantes : •    Élaboration du calendrier des cours et ateliers •    Suivi des différentes étapes de la formation •    Organisation des séances du Comité directeur et/ou du Comité formation •    Préparation de l’ordre du jour et prise de PV •    Gestion des inscriptions et des participant·e·s au MAS et aux CAS ◦    Réponses aux demandes d’information des candidat·e·s au MAS et aux CAS ◦    Gestion et suivi des inscriptions des candidat·e·s au MAS et aux CAS ◦    Suivi des participant·e·s au MAS et aux CAS ◦    Transmission des informations sur le déroulement du programme ◦    Permanence pour les demandes des participant·e·s •    Gestion des intervenant·e·s du MAS et des CAS : ◦    Élaboration et suivi des contrats ◦    Élaboration des fiches d’indemnités et suivi des paiements ◦    Organisation des séjours des intervenant·e·s si besoin ◦    Permanence pour leurs demandes Promotion du programme en collaboration avec la FCUE Relation avec la FCUE et les partenaires des programmes de formations continues du MAS et des CAS (UNIFR, UNINE, UNIGE) Votre profil Nous souhaitons engager, afin de compléter notre équipe, une personne ayant le profil suivant : Formation universitaire Connaissances dans le domaine de la formation et du diplôme concerné Expérience dans la gestion administrative Très bon sens de la planification et de l’organisation Esprit méthodique et précision Excellente maîtrise des outils informatiques Excellentes compétences à communiquer et à collaborer au sein d’une équipe Excellentes capacités de rédaction en français Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié Des possibilités de formation continue Des possibilités de télétravail Un accès facilité à un centre sportif sur le site de Dorigny Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Claire Leeming – Directrice exécutive de la formation claire.leeming@unil.ch Pour plus d’informations sur le MAS et les CAS en MRHC : https://www.mrhc.ch Délai de candidature 13.09.2026 Nous vous prions de bien vouloir nous transmettre votre dossier complet en format Word ou PDF.  Il ne sera pris en compte que les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site. Nous vous remercions de votre compréhension. Cahier des charges du poste Cahier des charges Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22942&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=MqVOJaeoN3APO%2flh%2fVEWrlAmhKgIZ69zWj4GfpPWhX0%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry (22942)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry (22942) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry (22942) Requisition ID 22942 - Posted 08/25/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Institute of Earth Surface Dynamics ( IDYST ) is inviting applications for a fully-funded Ph.D position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry within the Hydrology group (Principal Investigator : Prof. Paolo Benettin). Job information Expected start date in position : 01.01.2027/ to be agreed Contract length : 1 year initially, extension up to 4 years Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Lausanne Mouline (Géopolis building) Your responsibilities The Ph.D. candidate will design and perform a series of experiments at the Unil Ecotron facility , to investigate how vegetation regulates soil water fluxes and geochemical reactions , expecially during dry periods. The facility already includes a programmable climate chamber with three soil columns and a range of sensors, and additional sensors can be acquired during the project. Depending on the candidate's interests and skills, the work may combine a range of methods, including analyses of major and trace elements, measurements of vegetation activity, tracer experiments and hydrogeochemical modelling. As climate change increases the frequency and severity of droughts, this Ph.D. project offers the opportunity to understand and anticipate drought impacts on water resources and ecosystem degradation, while developing expertise at the interface of hydrology, soil geochemistry, and ecosystem science. 80% of the employment time will be dedicated to completing the doctoral thesis (PhD research); the remaining 20% will be dedicated to teaching assistant and support duties within the institute. You are expected to : Design and conduct innovative experiments Operate the Ecotron facility and its network of ~80 sensors throughout the project Lead scientific articles in international peer-reviewed journals Participate in international conferences and project meetings in lausanne and Paris Participate in approximately one week of fieldwork per year at the Critical Zone Observatory of Mt Lozère, France Make your research workflow (data, code, protocols...) open and reproducible Openly discuss research obstacles and seek advice/help in the group Actively participate in creating a collaborative and inclusive culture Your qualifications Background in disciplines like Environmental Science, Soil Science/Physics, Biogeochemistry, Experimental Ecology, Hydrology, Civil/Environmental Engineering, or closely related disciplines. Previous experience with experimental work. Examples may include deploying sensors, collecting soil/water/vegetation samples from the field, conducting laboratory analyses. Strong quantitative and data handling skills (e.g. in R or Python). Good written and spoken English communication skills. Knowledge of French is an asset but is not required. What the position offers you Annual salary of CHF 55'000 for up to 4 years (until graduation). A friendly and cohesive culture at the Institute of Earth Surface Dynamics ( IDYST ) including 1-day Summer and Winter retreats, usually in the Alps. A shared office in the pleasent Géopolis building, on campus. Fully-funded personal research equipment (laptop, desktop computer, monitor, etc.) and research-related travel (conferences, collaborations, etc.). Opportunity for co-supervision of the Ph.D. program by a second Principal Ingestigator. International collaboration network and opportunities to spend research periods abroad. Opportunity (but not obligation) to attend doctoral schools and take classes. Access to laboratories and platforms (analytical platform, geochemistry, stable isotopes) as well as workshops (wood, metal, 3D print). Support in your future career choices, throug the IDYST Careers group and Graduate Campus activities. Access to Unil Campus facilities (Sports center with 100+ recreational options, restaurants, etc). 5 weeks of paid holidays (in addition to 1 week of national holidays) and Paid Parental leave . The University of Lausanne is committed to equal opportunity and stands firm against all forms of discrimination. The Faculty of Geosciences and Environment of the University of Lausanne adheres to the DORA agreement and follows its guidelines in the evaluation of applications (in short-quality over quantity). Contact for further information All questions related to the application can be adressed by email to the Unil Hydrology Group : hydrology@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 30.09.2026 Please, send the following document in PDF format : Motivation letter (strict max 2 pages), including : Your professional goals in the next 6-7 years, and how this position might further them A ~250-word description of a topic you felt passionate about in the last ~2 years Description of the methods you feel more comfortable with and why (e.g. numerical modeling, sensor deployment, sample collection, lab analysis, statistics, spatial analyses, programming, etc.) A disclosure of how Artificial Intelligence was used to prepare your application Short Curriculum Vitae (max 2 pages) Copy of all university degree certificates and transcripts Copy of one first-author research report (can be a manuscript, a thesis, or an assignment report) Names, affiliations, and emails addresses of at least 2 references (e.g. Master thesis advisor, academic staff who have read your work, previous employers) Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22958&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=MqVOJaeoN3APO%2flh%2fVEWrlAmhKgIZ69zWj4GfpPWhX0%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral (Premier Assistant) position in Evolutionary Biology (22958)",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral (Premier Assistant) position in Evolutionary Biology (22958) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral (Premier Assistant) position in Evolutionary Biology (22958) Requisition ID 22958 - Posted 08/24/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The group of Prof. Alexandre Roulin is proposing a Postdoctoral (Premier Assistant) position in Evolutionary Biology at the Department of Ecology and Evolution, University of Lausanne, Switzerland. The postdoc will join a dynamic team working mainly on conservation biology in evolutionary biology. For more information, see https://www.chouette-effraie.ch/en Job information Expected start date in position : 01.01.2027 Contract length : 1 year, renewable depending on funding availability Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Lausanne-Dorigny Your responsibilities The research project will be defined together with the group leader based on the Postdoc interests and competences in the field of population ecology. Most of his/her time will be dedicated to research, but a contribution to teaching is expected, including the possibility of supervising master students. The job description stipulates: 70% Personal research; 25% Participation to teaching activities and master student supervision; 5% Maintenance of lab equipment or other institutional tasks. Your qualifications We are seeking to recruit someone with a strong interest and a PhD degree in biology, with skills in population dynamics. Experience with R would be an advantage. The applicants should have a strong ability to work in a team as PhD students are also involved in this project. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. The Department of Ecology and Evolution in Lausanne University hosts research groups working on a broad range of topics, producing a rich intellectual and social life. Although French is the common language in Lausanne region, the department research activities and seminars are conducted in English. The campus is located on the shore of the Leman Lake, with the view on the Alps. Contact for further information For further information please contact Prof. Alexandre Roulin : Alexandre.Roulin@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 30.09.2026 Formal applications should include: a cover letter detailing your research interests, experience and motivation for applying; your CV; a copy of your PhD certificate (or when you will get it); the names of two or three referees. To receive full consideration, application documents should be uploaded online through the University of Lausanne recruitment platform. Review of applications will begin immediately. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    }
  },
